 "music_pan": "Amiga: channels 0+3 left, 1+2 right",
 "notes": "Triggers from re/out/hunter_en_800.disasm.txt + names.txt + the SFX driver disassembly (tools/audio/disasm_sfx.py). Mechanism: the game calls PlaySound $B11C (d4 = sound = effect index) -> AllocChannel $2D30 -> SetChannel $B12A which writes the request byte to soundfile+$2D2+channel, the volume to +$2D6+channel and a period word to the channel record; the SFX driver's tick $113A6 consumes the request and plays effect[k] (sample/envelope/period/duration at $1178C+16k) - verified in the driver code at $11412-$11438. Entity (engine) sounds: StartEntitySound $2CD6 with d4 = entity +$88 & $1F. AmbientSound $B08E with volume $1F. Game volume for one-shots is 63 (not 64), so rendered peaks are ~1.5% above what the chip would output. Priority table $B164: sounds 0-5 -> 1-3, 6 -> 6, 7-14 -> 4, 15-20 -> 5.",
 "output_rate_hz": 44100,
 "pal_clock": 3546895,
